# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirect rules.
#
# Only the permanent legacy aliases live here. There is deliberately NO
# `/*` catch-all: both Cloudflare Pages and Netlify serve /404.html
# automatically for any path that does not match a file, and on Cloudflare
# Pages a catch-all rule is unsupported as a rewrite and — because Pages
# applies _redirects rules even when a static asset matches the request —
# risks hijacking asset requests (/assets/*.js would arrive as text/html
# and the app would never boot: grey screen).
#
# The 404 page is generated into dist/404.html by scripts/prerender.mjs,
# which fails the build if it is missing.
/dashboard            /                     301
/overview             /                     301
/logs                 /research-notes       301
/logs/*               /research-notes/:splat 301
/lab-logs             /research-notes       301
/bench                /acoustic-bench       301
/spectra              /spectra-lab          301
/oculus               /void-oculus          301
/synthesis            /synthesis-signal     301
/legal                /legal/institutional-status 301
/infrastructure       /field-stations       301
/vault                /post-mortems         301
/failures             /post-mortems         301
/personnel            /fellows              301
/personnel/*          /fellows/:splat       301
/audit                /system-audit         301
